#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:38
msgid "Alt text describes each image's purpose"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:38
msgid "Open the Media Library and read the alt text of your key images. It should say what the image shows or does in context, not just repeat the file name. Purely decorative images should have empty alt text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:39
msgid "Videos have accurate captions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:39
msgid "Play each video with captions on. Captions should match the speech and include important sounds. Auto-generated captions usually need correcting."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:40
msgid "Videos describe important visual information"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:40
msgid "If a video shows information only visually (on-screen text, actions), it needs narration or an audio-described version."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:41
msgid "Reading order makes sense"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:41
msgid "Turn off page styles (or use reader view) and read the page top to bottom. Content should still appear in a logical order."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:42
msgid "Instructions don't rely on shape, color, size or position alone"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:42
msgid "Look for instructions like \"click the green button\" or \"see the box on the right\" and add a text label to them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:43
msgid "Color is not the only way information is shown"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:43
msgid "Links in body text, required form fields, errors and chart data should also use underlines, text, icons or patterns."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:44
msgid "Tooltips and pop-ups on hover can be dismissed and hovered"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:44
msgid "Content that appears on hover or focus must close with Escape, stay open while the pointer moves onto it, and not vanish on its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:45
msgid "Everything works with a keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:45
msgid "Put the mouse away. Use Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, Space and arrow keys to use menus, forms, sliders, tabs and pop-ups."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:46
msgid "Keyboard focus never gets stuck"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:46
msgid "While tabbing, make sure you can always move focus out of every component, including embedded videos, maps and chat widgets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:47
msgid "Focus moves in a logical order"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:47
msgid "Tab through each page template. Focus should follow the visual order, and open dialogs should receive focus."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:48
msgid "Headings and labels are descriptive"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:48
msgid "Each heading should tell you what the section is about, and each form label should say what to enter."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:49
msgid "Focused items aren't hidden behind sticky headers or banners"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:49
msgid "Tab through pages with a sticky header, cookie banner or chat button visible. The focused element must stay at least partly visible."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:50
msgid "Anything you drag can also be done without dragging"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:50
msgid "Sliders, sortable lists and maps need a click or tap alternative, such as buttons."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:51
msgid "Navigation is consistent across pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:51
msgid "Menus and repeated links should appear in the same order on every page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:52
msgid "Form errors are clearly described in text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:52
msgid "Submit each form with mistakes. Every error should be explained in text next to the field, not only with a red border."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:53
msgid "Form errors suggest how to fix them"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:53
msgid "Error messages should say what is expected, for example \"Enter a date as DD/MM/YYYY\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:54
msgid "Users don't have to re-enter the same information"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:54
msgid "In multi-step forms or checkout, information entered earlier should be filled in or selectable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:55
msgid "Login doesn't require solving a puzzle or memorizing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:55
msgid "Login and account forms should allow password managers and paste, and avoid puzzle CAPTCHAs without an alternative."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:56
msgid "Status messages are announced to screen readers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:56
msgid "Messages like \"Added to cart\" or \"Form sent\" should be announced without moving focus. Test with a screen reader."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:57
msgid "One page tested with a screen reader"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:57
msgid "Use NVDA (Windows, free) or VoiceOver (Mac/iPhone, built in) to navigate your home page and one form. Note anything confusing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-compare.php:30
msgid "One of the audits could not be found."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-dismiss.php:32
msgid "Not a real problem (false positive)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-dismiss.php:33
msgid "Already accessible in a way the scan can't see"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-dismiss.php:34
msgid "Known issue, accepted for now"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-dismiss.php:67
msgid "That issue could not be found."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-editor.php:60
msgid "Check this element against the WCAG requirement shown, then update it in the block settings or ask your theme or plugin developer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:29
msgid "A screen reader instruction (ARIA) is used incorrectly"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:30 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:71 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:77 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:83 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:89 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:95 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:132 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:138 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:156 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:162 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:168 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:198 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:204 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:210 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:217 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:223 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:265 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:271 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:277 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:289 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:313
msgid "Screen reader users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:31
msgid "ARIA attributes tell assistive technology what an element is and what state it is in. When they are wrong or incomplete, screen readers announce confusing or false information, which can be worse than having no ARIA at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:32
msgid "Check the element's role and aria-* attributes against the expected pattern. Often the simplest fix is to use a native HTML element (button, link, input) instead of ARIA. This usually comes from a theme or plugin, so you may need to contact its developer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:36
msgid "Accessibility problem"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:37
msgid "People using assistive technology"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:38
msgid "This element does not meet a WCAG requirement, which can make it hard or impossible for some visitors to perceive or use."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:39
msgid "Open \"How to fix this\" for detailed guidance on this rule, then update the element in your content, theme or plugin settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:52
msgid "Images are missing a text description"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:53
msgid "Blind and low-vision visitors using screen readers; also search engines"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:54
msgid "Screen readers read an image's alt text out loud. Without it, visitors hear only \"image\" or the file name, so they miss whatever the picture shows or does."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:55
msgid "Add alt text that describes what the image shows or does, in a short sentence. If the image is purely decorative, give it empty alt text so screen readers skip it. In WordPress, set this in the Media Library or the image block's settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:58
msgid "Images in your posts are missing a text description"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:59 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:65
msgid "Blind and low-vision visitors using screen readers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:60
msgid "This image was found in post content without any alt attribute, so screen readers have nothing to announce."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:61
msgid "Edit the post, select the image and fill in \"Alternative text\" in the block settings. Use empty alt text only for decorative images."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:64
msgid "Media Library images have no alt text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:66
msgid "Alt text set in the Media Library is used automatically wherever the image is inserted later. Leaving it empty means every future use starts without a description."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:67
msgid "Go to Media > Library, open the image and fill in \"Alternative Text\". Leave it empty only if the image is purely decorative."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:70
msgid "Graphics marked as images have no description"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:72
msgid "This element is announced as an image but has no text alternative, so its meaning is lost."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:73
msgid "Add an aria-label or aria-labelledby that describes the graphic, or remove role=\"img\" if it is decorative."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:76
msgid "SVG images have no description"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:78
msgid "Icons and illustrations drawn as SVG need a text alternative just like regular images."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:79
msgid "Add a <title> inside the SVG or an aria-label on it. If the icon is decorative, add aria-hidden=\"true\" instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:82
msgid "Image buttons have no text alternative"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:84
msgid "A button made from an image needs alt text that says what the button does, or users won't know what will happen when they press it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:85
msgid "Add alt text describing the action, for example \"Search\" or \"Submit order\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:88
msgid "Clickable areas of an image map have no text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:90
msgid "Each clickable area works like a link and needs text saying where it goes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:91
msgid "Add alt text to every <area> element describing its destination."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:94
msgid "Embedded objects have no text alternative"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:96
msgid "Embedded content such as old plugins or documents needs a description so everyone knows what it contains."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:97
msgid "Add an aria-label or title to the <object>, or provide the content another way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:100
msgid "Text is hard to read against its background"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:101
msgid "People with low vision or color blindness, older visitors, anyone reading on a phone in sunlight"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:102
msgid "When text and background colors are too similar, the text fades out. WCAG asks for a contrast ratio of at least 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:103
msgid "Make the text darker or the background lighter (or the opposite on dark designs) until the ratio passes. You can usually change these colors in your theme's style settings or the block's color settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:106
msgid "Links in text can only be spotted by color"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:107
msgid "People with color blindness or low vision"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:108
msgid "If a link looks just like the surrounding text except for its color, some visitors can't tell it's a link."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:109
msgid "Underline links in body text, or give them enough contrast with the surrounding text plus a visible change on hover and focus."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:112
msgid "Links don't say where they go"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:113 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:119
msgid "Screen reader and voice control users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:114
msgid "This link has no readable text, often because it only contains an icon or an image without alt text. Screen readers announce it as just \"link\", and voice users can't say its name to click it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:115
msgid "Add visible link text, or alt text to the image inside the link, or an aria-label such as \"Read more about our services\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:118
msgid "Buttons have no name"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:120
msgid "A button with only an icon, or nothing at all, is announced as just \"button\". Visitors can't tell what it does."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:121
msgid "Give the button visible text, or an aria-label that describes its action, such as \"Open menu\" or \"Search\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:125
msgid "Form fields have no label"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:126
msgid "Screen reader users, people with cognitive disabilities, everyone filling in forms"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:127
msgid "Without a label, screen readers can't say what a field is for. Placeholder text alone disappears as soon as you type."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:128
msgid "Add a visible <label> connected to each field. Most form plugins have a \"label\" setting; make sure it isn't hidden or empty."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:131
msgid "Dropdown menus have no label"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:133
msgid "Screen readers can't say what a dropdown is for when it has no label."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:134
msgid "Add a visible label connected to the dropdown."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:137
msgid "Form fields have more than one label"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:139
msgid "Different screen readers pick different labels when a field has several, so some users hear the wrong one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:140
msgid "Keep one label per field and remove the extra ones."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:143
msgid "Form fields use an invalid autofill hint"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:144
msgid "People with motor or memory difficulties who rely on autofill"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:145
msgid "Correct autocomplete values let browsers fill in names, emails and addresses automatically. A wrong value breaks that help."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:146
msgid "Use a standard autocomplete value such as \"email\", \"name\" or \"postal-code\", or remove the attribute."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:149
msgid "The page doesn't say what language it is in"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:150
msgid "Screen reader users; translation tools"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:151
msgid "Screen readers use the page language to pick the right voice and pronunciation. Without it, text may be read with the wrong accent and become hard to understand."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:152
msgid "Make sure your theme prints the language on the <html> tag. In WordPress this comes from Settings > General > Site Language and the theme's language_attributes() call."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:155
msgid "The page language code is not valid"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:157
msgid "An unrecognized language code means screen readers can't choose the right pronunciation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:158
msgid "Use a valid code like \"en\", \"en-US\" or \"ur\". Check Settings > General > Site Language."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:161
msgid "A section uses an invalid language code"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:163
msgid "Parts of a page can be marked as another language, but the code must be valid for screen readers to switch voices."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:164
msgid "Correct the lang attribute on that element to a valid language code."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:167
msgid "The page declares two different languages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:169
msgid "The lang and xml:lang attributes disagree, so assistive technology may pick the wrong one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:170
msgid "Make both attributes match, or remove xml:lang."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:173
msgid "The page has no title"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:174
msgid "Screen reader users, people with many tabs open, search engines"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:175
msgid "The page title is the first thing a screen reader announces and what appears in the browser tab. Without it, visitors can't tell pages apart."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:176
msgid "Make sure your theme supports \"title-tag\" and every page has a descriptive title."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:179
msgid "There is no way to skip straight to the main content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:180 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:295
msgid "Keyboard and screen reader users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:181
msgid "Without a \"Skip to content\" link or proper page landmarks, keyboard users must tab through the whole menu on every single page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:182
msgid "Add a \"Skip to content\" link as the first focusable item, and wrap the main content in a <main> element. Many themes include this option."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:185
msgid "Zooming is blocked on mobile"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:186
msgid "People with low vision on phones and tablets"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:187
msgid "The page stops visitors from pinch-zooming, so people who need larger text can't enlarge it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:188
msgid "Remove \"user-scalable=no\" and any \"maximum-scale\" below 2 from the viewport meta tag in your theme."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:191
msgid "The page refreshes or redirects on a timer"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:192
msgid "Screen reader users, people who read slowly"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:193
msgid "Automatic refreshes can move people away before they finish reading and reset their place on the page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:194
msgid "Remove the timed refresh, or use a server redirect instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:197
msgid "Lists contain items that aren't list items"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:199
msgid "Screen readers announce how many items a list has and let users jump between them. Other elements placed directly inside the list break that structure."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:200
msgid "Make sure <ul> and <ol> contain only <li> elements directly. This often comes from a theme or menu plugin, so you may need to ask its developer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:203
msgid "List items are placed outside a list"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:205
msgid "A list item outside a list isn't announced as part of a group, so the structure is lost."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:206
msgid "Wrap <li> elements in a <ul> or <ol>."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:209
msgid "Definition lists are structured incorrectly"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:211
msgid "Terms and definitions must be paired correctly to be announced together."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:212
msgid "Make sure <dl> contains only <dt> and <dd> groups."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:216
msgid "Embedded content (iframes) has no title"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:218
msgid "Videos, maps and widgets embedded in frames need a title so visitors know what the embedded area contains before entering it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:219
msgid "Add a title attribute to the iframe, for example title=\"Map of our office location\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:222
msgid "Several embedded frames share the same title"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:224
msgid "Identical titles make it impossible to tell embedded areas apart."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:225
msgid "Give each iframe a unique, descriptive title."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:228
msgid "Interactive content inside a frame can't be reached by keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:229 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:253
msgid "Keyboard users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:230
msgid "The frame is removed from the tab order but contains things you can click, so keyboard users can't reach them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:231
msgid "Remove tabindex=\"-1\" from the iframe."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:234
msgid "Videos have no captions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:235
msgid "Deaf and hard-of-hearing visitors; anyone watching with the sound off"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:236
msgid "Without captions, everything said in the video is lost for people who can't hear it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:237
msgid "Add a captions track to the video (a .vtt file), or use a video host such as YouTube that supports edited captions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:240
msgid "Audio plays automatically"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:241
msgid "Screen reader users, people with attention or anxiety conditions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:242
msgid "Sound that starts on its own can drown out a screen reader, and visitors may not find how to stop it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:243
msgid "Turn off autoplay, or make sure it stops within 3 seconds and has a clear pause control."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:246
msgid "Clickable elements are placed inside other clickable elements"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:247 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:283
msgid "Screen reader and keyboard users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:248
msgid "A button inside a link (or similar) confuses assistive technology, and the inner control may never be announced or reachable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:249
msgid "Restructure the element so links and buttons are not nested inside each other."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:252
msgid "Scrollable areas can't be scrolled with a keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:254
msgid "Content in a scrolling box is out of reach if keyboard users can't move focus into the box."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:255
msgid "Add tabindex=\"0\" and an accessible name to the scrollable area, or make sure it contains a focusable element."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:258
msgid "Buttons or links are too small to tap easily"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:259
msgid "People with tremors or limited dexterity, everyone on a phone"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:260
msgid "Tiny targets packed close together lead to mis-taps. WCAG 2.2 asks for at least 24 by 24 pixels, or enough space around smaller targets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:261
msgid "Increase the size or padding of the link or button, or add more space between neighbouring targets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:264
msgid "Table cells point to headers that don't exist"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:266
msgid "Screen readers announce each cell's headers. Broken references mean cells are read without context."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:267
msgid "Make sure every id in a cell's headers attribute matches a header cell in the same table."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:270
msgid "Table headers don't describe any data"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:272
msgid "Header cells that don't relate to any data cells make the table structure confusing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:273
msgid "Use header cells only for real row or column headings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:276
msgid "Elements referenced by labels share the same id"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:278
msgid "When two elements have the same id, labels and descriptions may point to the wrong one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:279
msgid "Give every element a unique id."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:282
msgid "Hidden elements can still receive keyboard focus"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:284
msgid "The element is hidden from screen readers but can still be tabbed to, so users land on something that is announced as nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:285
msgid "Remove aria-hidden, or make the focusable items inside it unfocusable (for example with the inert attribute)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:288
msgid "The whole page is hidden from screen readers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:290
msgid "aria-hidden on the page body makes the entire site invisible to assistive technology."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:291
msgid "Remove aria-hidden=\"true\" from the <body> element. This is often left behind by a pop-up or menu script."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:294
msgid "Server-side image maps are used"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:296
msgid "Server-side image maps only work with a mouse."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:297
msgid "Replace it with regular links or a client-side image map with alt text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:300
msgid "Blinking content is used"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:301
msgid "People with attention or vision conditions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:302
msgid "Blinking text is distracting and hard to read, and can't be paused."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:303
msgid "Remove the <blink> element."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:306
msgid "Scrolling text (marquee) is used"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:307
msgid "People with attention, reading or vision conditions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:308
msgid "Moving text is hard to read and can't be paused."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:309
msgid "Replace the <marquee> with static text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:312
msgid "Expandable sections have no name"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:314
msgid "The toggle for an expandable section has no text, so visitors don't know what it opens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:315
msgid "Add text inside the <summary> element."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:335 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:336 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:337 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:338 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:339
msgid "Some images are missing a text description"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:340
msgid "Some text has low color contrast"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:341
msgid "Some links don't describe where they go"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:342
msgid "Some buttons have no accessible name"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:343
msgid "Some form fields have no label"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:344 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:345
